==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Bloody Jack''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Lightning Jack''' at level 30 with [[Catfruit]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
Thunder Jack is meant to be used as a rusher, with his rapid attacks essentially stunlocking enemies within his target traits if his knockback activates. He has the rare combination of insane DPS and health, with no knockbacks to interrupt his flurry of punches. His incredible stats, combined with his Knockback ability and low cost and cooldown, make him a very aggressive pusher. He can use his high bulk to quickly infiltrate enemies, knocking them away and giving your team space. He can't reposition, but merely advancing your frontline is more than compensation, not to mention he himself is vulnerable to knockback and warp.

If used as a rushdown attacker, like [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]], he excels against a boss who can't be outranged anyway, so that he may just outdamage it. He can, for example, get up to [[Hannya]] and deliver damage uninterrupted until the latter takes a knockback, or do the same with [[Daboo of the Dead]], [[Sunfish Jones]] and so on, assuming he's defended. Ironically, it's best if he doesn't target the trait he's fighting against, if it is a long ranged boss. His speed allows him to also counter knockback-ensnaring enemies like [[H. Nah]] and [[Mr. Mole]], to a degree: he gets pushed away, but still jumps in for damage. Naturally, his pressure is also excellent against [[:Category:Long Distance Cats|Long Distance attackers]] in general, especially Henry in Thunder Jack's Evolved Form. On the other hand, his single-target attacks, short range and lack of knockbacks all contribute to make him non ideal against hordes, as he is likely to be overwhelmed and die very early. Speaking of knockbacks, against threats like [[Inumusha]] and [[King Wahwah]], Thunder Jack also excels, as due to his rapid attacks and their low health per knockback, they never get a chance to attack.

In terms of ability, Thunder Jack is able to push its targeted traits far back with ease, even in groups, with a knockback every 0.7 seconds on average (the slower the enemy, the bigger group can be handled). While [[:Category:Alien Enemies|Aliens]] have many tricks to prevent this, namely [[Barrier]]s or simply backliners with high damage or warp, there are still many who are rendered useless by Thunder Jack, none more than [[Cyberhorn]]. [[:Category:Angel Enemies|Angels]] usually have many knockbacks themselves and are often equipped with ways to make up for it, but [[:Category:Zombie Enemies|Zombies]] are a different story. Zombies can both burrow to resurface in an inconvenient position and die to revive in an inconvenient positions; as for Jack... his unrivaled knockback frequency makes him exceptional at getting enemies away from inconvenient positions and back to the frontline, resulting in a pretty excellent counter, not to mention the chance to interrupt burrows as they happen. Unfortunately, the surprising lack of Zombie Killer also means that Jack may himself cause the aforementioned deaths that result in inconvenient revives.

As a unit with deep reliance on both attack power and health, Jack is the type of unit that would benefit the most from a high level, so it is recommended to upgrade him as much as possible, if planning to use him.

Side note: his lack of knockbacks and high health may even allow him to be warped so far left by [[Mesocosmocyclone]]s that he can clip the enemy base and attack it from further left than enemies can spawn (which basically means he can destroy it from where enemies will never reach). He's not the only one capable of performing this trick, but arguably the best for the job.

==='''True Form'''===
'''Lightning Jack''' is unfortunately a lackluster True Form due to a lack of [[Shield Piercing]], which prevents him from constantly destroying the [[:Category:Aku Enemies|Aku]] that he switches the [[:Category:Zombie Enemies|Zombie]] target out for. Most relevant Aku enemies have extremely durable [[Shield]]s that block status effects, and his raw force does little to mitigate it compared to [[:Category:Shield Piercing Cats|Shield Piercer]]s, especially considering unlike Barriers, Shields can regenerate on a handful of relevant threats. Regardless, he becomes a monster at handling Aku with no or weak Shields like [[Aku Gory]], [[Fallen Bear]], [[Medu-san]] and [[Midnite D.]]

[[Immune to Surge|Surge Immunity]] is great on [[Surge Attack|Surge]]-heavy stages, making him an effective [[:Category:Cats with Surge Immunity|Surge-immune]] rusher alongside [[Idi:N (Special Cat)|Idi:N2]] and [[Issun Boshi (Uber Rare Cat)|Kozuchimaru]] in a variety of stages.

