==Trivia==
*Thunder Jack's Japanese description states that he received his powers after being struck by lightning. This could be a reference to the DC character [[wikipedia:Captain Marvel (DC Comics)|Shazam]], who is able to transform after being hit by a lightning strike.
*Thunder Jack's name and possibly design may be inspired by [[wikipedia:Raiden (Metal Gear)|Raiden]] from the ''[[wikipedia:Metal Gear|Metal Gear]]'' series. Both have white hair, are named Jack, and have the ability to use electricity. Thunder Jack's attack animation may also be a nod towards the fight between Raiden and Senator Steven Armstrong, where Raiden does a flurry of punches that are the same color as Thunder Jack's.
*Thunder Jack resembles [[wikia:onepunchman:Blast|Blast]] from  ''[[wikipedia:One-Punch Man|One-Punch Man]]''. Both have a similar cape, similar sunglasses, a generally similar outfit and fight by punching with their gauntlets.
*Bloody Jack's description is likely a reference to a trope in Japanese media where places, usually schools, have a unique "[https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/TheSevenMysteries seven mysteries]", usually supernatural events.

